nventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MONDEN RYUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NITOH HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHATA HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKABE TOSHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIRANE KORO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUTA, YUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MONDEN, RYUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NITOH, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHATA, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKABE, TOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIRANE, KORO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A solid electrolytic capacitor having a masking structure by which the anode is reliably insulated from the cathode, a method for producing the same, a method and device for applying a masking material to the substrate of such a solid electrolytic capacitor are disclosed. A masking material fully covers a dielectric coating on a metallic member having a valve action and penetrates sufficiently to the core metal having a valve action. Therefore the solid electrolyte is completely masked with the masking material, thus producing a solid electrolytic capacitor which causes little leak current and in which the stress produced during the reflow processing is relaxed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un condensateur électrolytique solide présentant une structure de masquage selon laquelle l'anode est isolée de la cathode de manière fiable. Cette invention concerne également un procédé de fabrication de ce condensateur, ainsi qu'un procédé et un dispositif permettant d'appliquer un corps de masquage au substrat d'un condensateur électrolytique solide de ce type. Un corps de masquage recouvre entièrement un revêtement diélectrique formé sur un élément métallique d'actionnement de soupape, ce corps pénétrant suffisamment dans le noyau métallique destiné à actionner une soupape. L'électrolyte solide est donc totalement masqué par ledit corps de masquage, ce qui permet d'obtenir un condensateur électrolytique solide ne causant qu'un courant de fuite de faible intensité, et dans lequel la contrainte exercée au cours du traitement par refusion est réduite.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>